# Example Commit Messages
# =======================


# ─── Example: Simple refactor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# refactor(card-generator): rename generateCardDetails to generateCard
#
# Improve code readability. The original name was overly verbose and redundant with the class name.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤


# ─── Example: Simple docs change ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# docs: clarify setup instructions in README.md
#
# Fixes #12
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤


# ─── Example: A bug fix ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# fix(boot-sequence): ensure progress bar reaches 100% before boot completes
#
# Previously, fast timing configurations caused the progress calculation to overflow before the
# complete callback was registered.
#
# Now we sanitize timing bounds and guarantee clean completion triggers.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤


# ─── Example: A test enhancement ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# test(system7-desktop): add unit tests for localStorage layout restoration
#
# Adds coverage for window position restoration and invalid JSON fallback handling.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤


# ─── Example: Breaking change ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# feat(sound-effects): migrate WebAudio engine to modern AudioWorklet nodes
#
# Legacy ScriptProcessorNode is deprecated and causes audio stuttering under high UI render load.
#
# BREAKING CHANGE: sound-effects service constructor now requires AudioContext initialization options.
#
# Update instantiation calls to pass explicit AudioContextOptions configuration objects.
#
# Fixes #42
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤



# Bit-Hack Commit Message Format
# ==============================
#
# This repository follows the Conventional Commits specification modeled after Angular's guidelines.
#
# Each commit message consists of a *header*, a *body*, and a *footer*.
#
# <header>
# <BLANK LINE>
# <body>
# <BLANK LINE>
# <footer>
#
# The header is mandatory.
#
# The body is mandatory for all commits except for simple docs/test commits.
# When required, explain WHY the change was made.
#
# The footer is optional.
#
# Lines in the commit message body should not exceed 100 characters.
#
#
# Commit Message Header
# ---------------------
#
# <type>(<scope>): <short summary>
#   │       │             │
#   │       │             └─⫸ Summary in imperative, present tense ("add", "fix", "change").
#   │       │                Lower-case, no period at end.
#   │       │
#   │       └─⫸ Commit Scope (Examples):
#   │             Components: card-generator | boot-sequence | system7-desktop | status-bar |
#   │                         sound-control-panel | benchmark-modal | about-modal |
#   │                         retro-alert-modal | mac-window | console-log
#   │             Services:   sound-effects | card-generator-service
#   │             Core/Other: app | core | deps | test | build | ci | docs
#   │
#   └─⫸ Commit Type: build | ci | docs | feat | fix | perf | refactor | style | test
#
#
# Commit Message Body
# -------------------
#
# Use imperative, present tense: "fix" not "fixed" nor "fixes".
# Explain the motivation for the change. Explain WHY you are making the change and how it impacts
# the application compared to previous behavior.
#
#
# Commit Message Footer
# ---------------------
#
# Breaking changes should start with "BREAKING CHANGE: " followed by a summary, blank line, and
# migration instructions.
#
# ```
# BREAKING CHANGE: <breaking change summary>
# <BLANK LINE>
# <breaking change description + migration instructions>
# <BLANK LINE>
# Fixes #<issue number>
# ```
